---

bhgraph depends on nothing outside the Go standard library and reproduces no
third-party source code. Two third-party artifacts are present, and both are
data rather than code.

testdata/golden/mssqlhound-schema.json is internal/bloodhound/schema.json from
MSSQLHound (github.com/SpecterOps/MSSQLHound, Apache-2.0), redistributed
unmodified as a test fixture. MSSQLHound ships no NOTICE file of its own. It is
the only public reference implementation of a BloodHound extension definition
schema, and the suite round-trips it to check that our types lose no field
SpecterOps declares.

The fixed signature vectors in client/sign_test.go were produced by executing
BloodHound's reference implementation of the bhesignature scheme
(SpecterOps/BloodHound v9.5.1, cmd/api/src/api/signature.go, Apache-2.0) over
chosen inputs, and recording the resulting digests. The vectors are values, not
code: no BloodHound source is reproduced or distributed here. The provenance is
recorded because a test vector whose origin is undocumented looks more
authoritative than it is.
